{"title":"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Venn_Diagram)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Venn Diagram)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> students in the eighth grade at Lincoln Middle School has one dog or one cat or both a dog and a cat. Twenty students have a dog and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students have a cat. How many students have both a dog and a cat?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/513fb7702a630a38f4ab124528dbbc993da20153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 13\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 19\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 39\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"385\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The union of two sets is equal to the sum of each set minus their intersection. The number of students that have both a dog and a cat is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/482e3c9bffeb25fc1fce7b6ddd94da494af4f020.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20+26-39 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"179\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Venn_Diagram.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Venn_Diagram)\">Solution 2 (Venn Diagram)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Venn Diagram)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We create a diagram:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/0278976caa54753192763fd786ae0de7a7db44a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),5)); draw(circle((5,0),5)); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(2.3,0),S); label(&quot;$20$&quot;,(7,0),S); label(&quot;$26$&quot;,(-2,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of students with both a dog and a cat.\n</p><p>Therefore, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/375e63084c9d655639e4cbc1c30f0eda7ec8a1cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[26+20-x = 39\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/c/62c38cca81668b09f0d7617cfe61f6f44c9d9d21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[46-x = 39\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4b62274f2fb755a8ff15d331a1c70c6e2f0b1f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~7}\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 8\">2008 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<b